{"sha":"d61a767d6842b530ffb532ddd5a3d233119aad40","node_id":"MDY6Q29tbWl0MjE0NjExOTk6ZDYxYTc2N2Q2ODQyYjUzMGZmYjUzMmRkZDVhM2QyMzMxMTlhYWQ0MA==","commit":{"author":{"name":"Pierre Ossman","email":"ossman@cendio.se","date":"2019-09-10T09:05:48Z"},"committer":{"name":"Pierre Ossman","email":"ossman@cendio.se","date":"2019-11-15T09:53:26Z"},"message":"Make ZlibInStream more robust against failures\n\nMove the checks around to avoid missing cases where we might access\nmemory that is no longer valid. Also avoid touching the underlying\nstream implicitly (e.g. via the destructor) as it might also no\nlonger be valid.\n\nA malicious server could theoretically use this for remote code\nexecution in the client.\n\nIssue found by Pavel Cheremushkin from Kaspersky Lab","tree":{"sha":"d2facc2d59760bdee45f66e4a07f30a8774efce7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CendioOssman/tigervnc/git/trees/d2facc2d59760bdee45f66e4a07f30a8774efce7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CendioOssman/tigervnc/git/commits/d61a767d6842b530ffb532ddd5a3d233119aad40","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CendioOssman/tigervnc/commits/d61a767d6842b530ffb532ddd5a3d233119aad40","html_url":"https://github.com/CendioOssman/tigervnc/commit/d61a767d6842b530ffb532ddd5a3d233119aad40","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CendioOssman/tigervnc/commits/d61a767d6842b530ffb532ddd5a3d233119aad40/comments","author":{"login":"CendioOssman","id":6640916,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NDA5MTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6640916?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CendioOssman","html_url":"https://github.com/CendioOssman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CendioOssman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CendioOssman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CendioOssman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_